#Git
--------
->Git is a version control.
->Track all the changes even if you make changes.
->It has a work directory,- is where you make changes on.
->It also have a staging area/index where changes is
  prepared before commiting them it allow review of changes before making it part of the project history.
->Local repository is project history story on local computer, it includes the commits, and branches.
  It act as a personal record of the project changes
->Remote repositry is version of your project hosted on the internet or network. It allow multiple people to collaborate,
by pushing to pulling from the shared resource.
->Branches are parallel version of your project.
 They allow fixing different feature and fixes independently, without affecting the main project, until it is ready to match it back.
->Pull request is the way to propose changes from one branch to another.
-Merging is integrating changed from one branch into another. It combine the hostories of both branches creating a single unified history.

configuration the git
-----------------------

-configure user name - git config  --global user.name "username"
-configure uder email - git config --global user.email "useremail"
-git config --global alias.init


Common git commands and what they do
--------------------------------------

-git config --list - check last configuration.
-git init - create a git repository locally, first command to run in a new project.
-git status - allow tracking of changes.
-git add . - add all changes from the working directory to the staging area,
git commit -m "describe change you made" - store a version of your project  in the git history
-git clone - make a copy of a project from a remote storage to your local machine.

github
-----------

-Github is a platform that allow developers to collaborate on a project and store their code in the cloud.
-Git and github work together to make building, scaling,securing and storing software much easier.


Top git command
----------------
- git checkout -b branch-name - create branch 
git branch - list branches
- git switch branch-name - facilitate switching from one branch to another.
